 {"id": "electron-item-utility-processes",
  "kind": "out-of-scope",
  "reason": "TS runs each Agent chat and terminal in its own Electron UtilityProcess supervised by Main: process admission budgets (CPU, memory, per-project leases), heartbeats and liveness probes, crash replacement after cleanup confirmation, model leases per host, an item lifecycle supervisor with termination receipts and generations, instance RPC with byte bounds, MessagePort session connections bound to frames, and a renderer execution client that adapts them. The native app runs Agent sessions on its in-process Agent host thread and terminals on PTY workers owned by the window, so none of these process boundaries, leases or receipts exist; the in-process equivalents (closing, stale generations, late startup after close) are covered by the agent service, controller and workbench tests.",
